  urldate = {2026-07-02},
  abstract = {In the medical and health community, EEG signals are the most utilized signals in the clinical assessment of brain states, detection of epileptic seizures and identification of mental states for BCI systems. A reliable automatic classification and detection system would help to ensure an objective assessment thus facilitating treatments, and it would significantly improve the diagnosis of epilepsy. EEG signals could also be used for the long-term monitoring and treatment of patients. This chapter also provides a description of the experimental databases and performance evaluation measures used in this research. Furthermore, this chapter discusses the commonly used methods of EEG signal classification.},
